<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ōtomo Sōrin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1530–1587</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ōtomo Yoshishige, Otomo Sorin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ōtomo Sōrin, born Ōtomo Yoshishige, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of Bungo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> who led his clan from 1550. He welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-xavier">Francis Xavier</a> in 1551, traded with the Portuguese and was baptised in 1578, becoming one of the best-known Christian lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. After defeat by the Shimazu at Mimikawa he sought help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, whose invasion of Kyushu in 1587 saved his house.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otomo-sorin.jpg" alt="Ōtomo Sōrin" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otomo_Sorin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
